Subject: gpu: Fix ScopedBufferReattacher backbuffer restoration

In the validating GLES2 decoder (GLES2DecoderImpl), client framebuffer
0 is tracked as null in bound_read_framebuffer / bound_draw_framebuffer,
but is backed in the GL driver by the emulated backbuffer service ID
returned by GetBackbufferServiceId() (non-zero for offscreen contexts
and surfaces with backing FBOs), not raw driver FBO 0.

All canonical framebuffer binding restoration paths (DoBindFramebuffer,
RestoreCurrentFramebufferBindings, RestoreFramebufferBindings) map null
tracked bindings to GetBackbufferServiceId(). However, the driver
workaround helper ScopedBufferReattacher had two issues:

1. Its destructor mapped null tracked framebuffer bindings to raw driver
   FBO 0 instead of GetBackbufferServiceId(). When triggered by an
   unbound FBO while client FBO 0 was bound (under workarounds
   reattach_fbo_depth_stencil_on_reallocation or
   reattach_texture_to_fbo_after_layer_increase), ~ScopedBufferReattacher
   left the driver bound to raw FBO 0 while the state tracker believed
   the emulated backbuffer was bound. Subsequent operations such as
   CheckFramebufferValid(nullptr) would then issue pending lazy
   backbuffer clears (backbuffer_needs_clear_bits_) against driver FBO 0
   instead of the backbuffer while unconditionally disarming the clear
   bits.
2. Initialize() bound detached FBO service IDs in the driver to detach
   textures/renderbuffers without restoring the previous FBO bindings
   before returning. For commands like DoCopyTexImage2D where
   ScopedBufferReattacher is constructed before
   CheckBoundReadFramebufferValid() and glCopyTexImage2D(), this left
   the detached FBO bound in the driver during command execution.

Fix both issues by extracting ScopedBufferReattacher::RestoreBindings(),
which maps null tracked read/draw FBOs to GetBackbufferServiceId(), and
calling it at the end of both Initialize() (when attachments are
detached) and ~ScopedBufferReattacher(). Add unit tests verifying that
both shared and separate read/draw emulated backbuffer bindings are
properly restored across Initialize(), CopyTexImage2D lazy clears, and
destruction.

